','<p>Hi Michael,</p><p>Thank you for taking the time to meet with us on Friday, July 24, 2026. Here\'s a summary of our discussion and agreed next steps:</p><h3>Key Points Discussed</h3><ul><li>Pricing-indexing records are creating significant system load because pricing is approximately 99.5% identical across 40 groups, resulting in substantial record duplication.</li><li>A subgroup-based approach was discussed to consolidate identical pricing while preserving differences where required.</li><li>Groups are also used for location-based product visibility, with locations seeing a limited product list rather than the full catalog.</li><li>The proposed 2.4.7 system upgrade is expected to reduce the implementation estimate by approximately 50 hours.</li><li>Updated price-import logic is being tested and now limits reindexing to SKUs with modified prices. Preliminary results indicate faster processing.</li></ul><h3>Decisions Made</h3><ul><li>Technopath will prepare an estimate and recommended action plan for the proposed pricing-performance optimization.</li><li>Technopath will investigate whether product visibility requires configuration differences that should be preserved separately from pricing logic.</li><li>Technopath will send the revised 2.4.7 upgrade proposal reflecting the reduced effort forecast.</li><li>Create Pharmacy will complete additional validation of the updated price-import logic before providing approval to proceed.</li></ul><h3>Action Items</h3><ul><li><strong>Jean Paul Hanna:</strong> Prepare and send an estimate for the proposed pricing-performance optimization. <em>Due date: To be confirmed.</em></li><li><strong>Jean Paul Hanna:</strong> Research the product visibility requirements and identify any differentiators that require separate configuration logic. <em>Due date: To be confirmed.</em></li><li><strong>Jean Paul Hanna:</strong> Send the revised proposal and documentation for the 2.4.7 system upgrade, including the approximately 50-hour reduction. <em>Due date: To be confirmed.</em></li><li><strong>Romano:</strong> Complete additional testing of the updated price-import logic and report the findings to the development team. <em>Due date: To be confirmed.</em></li><li><strong>Create Pharmacy:</strong> Review the optimization estimate and upgrade proposal once received, and provide approval or feedback. <em>Due date: To be confirmed.</em></li></ul><h3>Open Questions</h3><ul><li>What specific product visibility requirements or differentiators must be preserved in the proposed subgroup solution?</li><li>What is the final estimate and recommended implementation plan for the pricing-performance optimization?</li><li>Will the additional price-import testing confirm that the updated logic is ready for production?</li></ul><h3>Next Steps / Next Meeting</h3><p>Technopath will provide the requested estimate, visibility findings, and 2.4.7 upgrade proposal. Create Pharmacy will complete testing and review the materials once received. No follow-up meeting was scheduled; next steps can be coordinated after these items are available.</p><p>Please don\'t hesitate to reach out if anything needs clarification.</p><p>Best,</p><p>Technopath</p>','Meeting Summary and Next Steps – Create Pharmacy','<p>Hi Michael,</p><p>Thank you for taking the time to meet with us on Friday, July 24, 2026. Here\'s a summary of our discussion and agreed next steps:</p><h3>Key Points Discussed</h3><ul><li>Pricing-indexing records are creating significant system load because pricing is approximately 99.5% identical across 40 groups, resulting in substantial record duplication.</li><li>A subgroup-based approach was discussed to consolidate identical pricing while preserving differences where required.</li><li>Groups are also used for location-based product visibility, with locations seeing a limited product list rather than the full catalog.</li><li>The proposed 2.4.7 system upgrade is expected to reduce the implementation estimate by approxima