umn structure.\n\nTechnical Maintenance and Implementation\nFood safe icon implementation requires updates at the configurable product level, impacting 13 items.\nConfigurable product defaults require selection of the lowest-priced option.\nAutomated testing implementation estimated at 70 hours.\nBank transfer functionality update remains pending input from Muhammad.\n\nNext steps\n[Nour Ayman] Send Task List: Provide an Excel sheet containing current tasks, their priorities, and hours spent or estimates.\n[Irem Aydin] Update Priorities: Review the shared Excel sheet and define the priority levels for all listed tasks.\n[Benoit Courcelle] Check Category Order: Verify the category order on the website for the 3 countries to ensure it matches the new standardized order.\n[Nour Ayman] Bulk Update Titles: Perform a bulk update for the Italia product titles based on the provided list.\n[Nour Ayman] Share Screenshot: Send a screenshot regarding the product variant clicking issue on the product listing page.\n[The group] Inform Midsummer: Communicate the design decision regarding the flat non-clickable product variant thumbnails.\n[The group] Request Design: Ask the Midsummer team to create a new product page design.\n[Jean Paul Hanna] Provide Estimates: Calculate and provide estimates for the configurable product defaults implementation.\n[The group] Review Price Units: Review the list of product codes and requested price display changes to send to the development team.\n[Nour Ayman] Send Meeting Summary: Provide an email after every meeting detailing the monthly hours completed and the specific tasks being worked on.\n[Jean Paul Hanna] Investigate Category Definitions: Clarify how shop categories are currently defined and managed on the platform.\n[Irem Aydin] Reorganize Product Categories: Review and refine current product groupings to remove irrelevant categories and prioritize key items.\n\n\n\nWant to see more? View the full notes\n\n',NULL,'The Cambro/Technopath tea