e\": \"Irem Aydin\", \"is_customer_facing\": true}, {\"title\": \"Set up and share staging front-end and back-end credentials for Irem\", \"due_date\": \"2026-08-06\", \"owner_name\": \"Nour Ayman\", \"is_customer_facing\": false}]','\"The new cookie consent banner will remain live in production for now, with the option to revert to the previous version if issues arise.\\nThe banner was redesigned to appear at the bottom of the screen with the \'Allow all\' button on the right.\\nThe team will prioritize high and highest priority tasks before moving to medium and low priority items.\\nDeployments to production will be batched and done once per week (end of week / Friday).\\nThe FAQ extension bug must be fixed before implementing the approved vertical FAQ design.\\nAsana links (rather than newly created help desk tickets) will be added to the tracking sheet for Asana-based tasks.\\nThe tracking sheet will be enhanced with ticket numbers, request dates, estimated times, and brief detail notes.\\nA Firebear tutorial/recording session will be held Monday, August 10 at 9:00 with Irem, Nour, and Donia.\\nStaging credentials were set up for Irem to run tests.\"','\"Should the \'Allow all\' button color be red (matching Cambro branding) or changed to blue? Awaiting Midsummer team feedback.\\nDoes the cookie consent banner need to be translated into German and Italian, and who will provide/approve the legal translations?\\nIs the AS400 to Magento stock sync updating correctly? To be confirmed with Cambro IT / Mike.\\nWill switching the color/size swatches affect the code-side tasks, or should Technopath focus on capacity swatches first?\\nWhy are some products missing from the exported Firebear file? May require a bug investigation.\\nWhether to copy the production database to staging so the full product catalog is available for testing (deprioritized unless deemed important).\"',NULL,'2026-08-05 18:38:33','cdikmen@cambro.com','[\"bcourcelle@cambro.com\", \"spaxia@cambro.com\", \"iaydin@cambro.com\", \"jp@technopath.co\", \"donia@technopath.co\"]','openrouter','anthropic/claude-opus-4.8',NULL,'2026-08-05 18:33:39',NULL,NULL,'2026-08-05 18:27:46','2026-08-05 18:38:33'),(7,247,'### Quick notes\n\nPlease rate the new Quick notes tab by taking a short survey.\n\nTranspart- Weekly Meeting\n\n\n   \n\nOperational updates concerning inventory core charges and international logistics and technical resolutions for customer communication systems.\n\nRecon Product Core Charges\nCore charges apply only to specific SKUs within the provided list of torque converters.\nManual updates per product suggested for applying core charges.\n\nShipStation International Shipping Setup\nNew UPS carrier account established specifically for international orders.\n\nSystem Maintenance and Chatbot Optimization\nOTP verification emails flagged for going to spam; migration to Klaviyo suggested for improved deliverability.\nBonded products kit deployment failures identified as a cluster-related technical issue.\nChatbot errors identified regarding irrelevant links, missing fitment responses, and incorrect query handling.\nProposed creating a structured interface in Retool to track chatbot performance, log errors, and define standardized response protocols (Jean Paul Hanna, Donia Attwa).\n\nDatabase and Part Number Alignment\nPart numbering undergoing continuous updates to align with current Retool and Transcend database formats.\nProduct fitment data availability confirmed within the Retool application.\n\nNext steps\n[Kelly Hufford] Process Core Charges: Apply relevant fees to the list of torque converters and return the updated document.\n[Nour Ayman] Check Core Charges: Review the manual process for adding costs to products and report any findings.\n[Donia Attwa] Configure UPS Carrier: Connect the new carrier account specifically for international orders and disconnect the previous one.\n[Jean Paul Hanna] Retrieve Product Data: Extract fit information from the retool and transcend databases.\n[Jean Paul Hanna, Donia Attwa] Design Training Interface: Develop a system to streamline chatbot training and response management.\n\n\nWant to see more? View the full notesTip: You can always access your full notes from the left sidebar.\n\n\n\nYou should review Gemini\'s notes to make sure they\'re accurate. Get tips and learn how Gemini takes notes\n\n### Full notes\n\nTranspart- Weekly Meeting\nInvited    \nAttachments \nMeeting records  \n\n\nSummary\nOperational updates concerning inventory core charges and international logistics and technical resolutions for customer communication systems.Inventory and Logistics UpdatesSystem updates will manually apply core charges for specific torque converter products. International shipping will transition to a new carrier integration via the existing logistics platform.Technical and Communication IssuesDeployment failures for bonded product kits are under investigation. Customer order status emails are routing to spam, prompting exploration of alternative communication platforms to improve deliverability.Chatbot Training and ImprovementThe team will document inaccurate chatbot responses regarding shipping and customer satisfaction in an external sheet to refine training. A new interface in the internal tool will be built to streamline data inputs.\n\n\nDecisions\nNeeds Further Discussion\nChatbot training interface implementation The team discussed using either a spreadsheet or Retool for chatbot training and agreed to evaluate the best interface before implementation.\n\nAligned\nManual core charge application process The team decided to apply core charges manually on a per-product basis within the system.\nNew UPS international carrier connection The team decided to connect the new UPS account specifically for international shipments and disconnect the previous carrier.\nChatbot OTP notification platform transition The team decided to utilize Klaviyo for sending OTP notifications if the current Zendesk ticket does not resolve the delivery issue.\nDevelopment of chatbot training process The team decided to create a tracking method to catalog bot errors and establish consistent training instructions for chatbot responses.\n\nWe\'ve updated the Decisions section using your feedback.\nLet us know what you think: Helpful or Not Helpful\n\n\nNext steps\n[Kelly Hufford] Process Core Charges: Apply relevant fees to the list of torque converters and return the updated document.\n[Nour Ayman] Check Core Charges: Review the manual process for adding costs to products and report any findings.\n[Donia Attwa] Configure UPS Carrier: Connect the new carrier account specifically for international orders and disconnect the previous one.\n[Jean Paul Hanna] Retrieve Product Data: Extract fit information from the retool and transcend databases.\n[Jean Paul Hanna, Donia Attwa] Design Training Interface: Develop a system to streamline chatbot training and response management.\n\n\nDetails\nRecon Products Core Charges: Nour introduced a list of torque converter products from the brand Recon for which core charges need to be applied (00:02:18). Kelly is responsible for reviewing the list and determining which specific Stock Keeping Units require these charges (00:03:18). Regarding the implementation, Jean Paul Hanna and Nour decided that the team will add the core charges manually on a per-product basis within the system (00:04:10).\nShipStation International Carrier Integration: Nour and Kelly discussed the addition of a new UPS account specifically designated for international shipping within ShipStation. Donia has been assigned the task of connecting this new carrier and disconnecting the previous international carrier, with a task already created to facilitate this work (00:05:11).\nBonded Products Kit Deployment Issue: Nour reported a technical issue regarding the bonded products kit, which is currently failing to deploy properly in the new cluster despite working correctly in the staging environment. Nour and the team are actively working on resolving this deployment failure (00:05:11).\nOrder Status One-Time Password Email Issue: Jean Paul Hanna and Nour addressed a problem where customers are not entering their One-Time Passwords to check order status because the verification emails are being routed to spam folders (00:06:15). Nour has submitted a support ticket to E-Desk to investigate the issue from their side. Alternatively, Jean Paul Hanna suggested integrating Klaviyo for sending these communications to leverage a better sending reputation and centralize customer interactions (00:07:14).\nChatbot Functionality - Irrelevant Responses: Kelly provided feedback regarding the AI chatbot, noting instances where it responded to customers who were expressing satisfaction with their purchases by providing irrelevant links to different kits (00:09:16). The team identified that these interactions serve as data points for training the chatbot to ensure it responds accurately and correctly identifies when a customer is not asking a question (00:10:25).\nChatbot Functionality - Shipping Inquiries: Kelly shared another instance where the chatbot failed to provide correct shipping information—such as information regarding UPS Next Day Air or Second Day Air services—when asked about the speed of delivery for specific Stock Keeping Units (00:10:25). To address these training gaps, Jean Paul Hanna decided that the team will create an external sheet to document these conversations, provide comments on the proper way to handle such inquiries, and establish instructions for when the chatbot should escalate a conversation to a support ticket (00:11:16).\nProduct Data Accuracy and Training Interface: Regarding product data, Kelly confirmed that accurate product descriptions and fitment information are available within the Retool application from Transcend and that the company is continuously updating part numbers to better align with that data (00:12:14). To streamline the chatbot training process, Jean Paul Hanna and Donia discussed the possibility of building an interface within Retool that would allow the team to input training data and instructions more efficiently (00:13:16).\n\n\nYou should review Gemini\'s notes to make sure they\'re accurate. Get tips and learn how Gemini takes notes\nHow is the quality of these specific notes? Take a short survey to let us know your feedback, including how helpful the notes were for your needs.','Transpart- Weekly Meeting - Transcript\n00:00:46\n\nDonia Attwa: Hi JP.\nJean Paul Hanna: Hi D. How are you?\nDonia Attwa: Good. How are you?\nJean Paul Hanna: Alhamdulillah. Hi, Kelly.\nKelly Hufford: Hello.\nJean Paul Hanna: How are you?\nKelly Hufford: Good. How are you?\nJean Paul Hanna: I\'m doing good. How you been?\nKelly Hufford: Good. Yeah. Nothing too much.\nJean Paul Hanna: Busy.\nKelly Hufford: Yeah. Yes. And no.\nJean Paul Hanna: It\'s It\'s good to be un busy sometime.\nKelly Hufford: Yes.\nJean Paul Hanna: We all deserve that.\nKelly Hufford: Are you ever unbusy?\nJean Paul Hanna: Um I\'ve been trying to be more lately.\nKelly Hufford: No.\nJean Paul Hanna: I\'m I\'m making an effort.\nNour Ayman: He can\'t.\nJean Paul Hanna: It\'s not as fun as as you do.\nNour Ayman: He can\'t. He can\'t. I pro I promise you he can\'t be un busy.\nJean Paul Hanna: What?\nKelly Hufford: Good.\nNour Ayman: Yes.\nJean Paul Hanna: How is that Nour?\nNour Ayman: Uh I\'m trying to be there. I\'m actually there.\nJean Paul Hanna: Yeah.\n\n\n00:02:18\n\nNour Ayman: But uh believe me, there\'s a lot of things like falling down.\nJean Paul Hanna: Yeah.\nKelly Hufford: What\'s up?\nNour Ayman: A lot of things.\nJean Paul Hanna: I think I think busy I think busy is a state of mind you know what I mean more than you know obviously busy there\'s a lot of things to do but you can\'t do everything\nNour Ayman: Yeah.\nJean Paul Hanna: all the time right so yeah I just try to do 