ium\"}, {\"key\": \"USG-1139\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Bulk Import\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-15T12:05:40.025-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Donia Khaled\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"USG-1075\", \"status\": \"Done\", \"summary\": \"Pepsi Partners Audit\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-15T12:05:30.372-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Donia Khaled\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}]}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'openrouter','~anthropic/claude-fable-latest',NULL,'2026-07-21 21:06:33',NULL,NULL,'2026-07-21 21:06:33','2026-07-21 21:06:33'),(4,188,'TRAN','project = TRAN AND updated >= \'2026-07-16\' ORDER BY updated DESC','TRANSPART – INTERNAL PRE-MEETING SUMMARY (Weekly Meeting, Tuesday, July 21, 2026, 11:00 PM)\n\nOVERALL PROJECT HEALTH: Moderate/Stable. Good delivery velocity this week (5 items completed, including the highest-priority AI Chatbot production deployment). However, the backlog is large (23 items in blocked/on-hold/backlog), and two high-priority items (TRAN-653, TRAN-491) remain in backlog with no visible movement. A security hotfix (TRAN-1286) is pending and should be prioritised.\n\nCOMPLETED SINCE LAST MEETING (5):\n- TRAN-1289: Reconcile out-of-stock flag with actual storefront behavior (Nour)\n- TRAN-1108: Code Review and Deployment (Mostafa)\n- TRAN-1107: Login as Customer redirect issue on production (Mostafa)\n- TRAN-1284: Deploy AI Chatbot to Production and Initialize Optimization – HIGHEST priority (Nour)\n- TRAN-1285: Dry run test (Nour)\n\nIN PROGRESS / READY FOR DEV (7):\n- TRAN-268: Project Management (Nour) – In Progress\n- TRAN-1281: Magento Catalog Update – Bundle & Configurable Products (JP) – In Progress\n- TRAN-1292: Merge eDesk accounts to support@tecnopath (Nour) – Ready For Dev\n- TRAN-1291: Check ShipStation and Klaviyo connections (Nour) – Ready For Dev\n- TRAN-1290: Analyze chatbot conversations with AI (Nour) – Ready For Dev\n- TRAN-1286: [Security] Hotfix CVE-2025-54236 (SessionReaper) on Adobe Commerce 2.4.7-p7 (Mostafa) – Ready For Dev. RISK: security patch should not sit in queue.\n- TRAN-1255: Product Kits Import Job failing at 90% (Mostafa) – Ready For Dev\n\nREADY FOR DEPLOYMENT (2):\n- TRAN-1275: Configure Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status Email Notifications (Mostafa)\n- TRAN-1283: Simplify Purchase Flow & Display for Rebuild Kits / Packages (Mostafa)\nBoth are candidates to walk the client through and confirm deployment timing/approval.\n\nBLOCKERS & RISKS:\n- TRAN-1027: Multiple \'True Orders\' on Staging / No Index-No Follow error – explicitly BLOCKED BY NEXCESS (third-party hosting dependency). Follow up with Nexcess.\n- TRAN-1071: Klaviyo 6-month campaign calendar – ON HOLD (Mahmoud). Confirm reason for hold and whether client input is needed to resume.\n- TRAN-653: Order Grid Row Coloring for UPS (MageWorx) – HIGHEST priority but still in BACKLOG (Leo). Needs prioritisation decision.\n- TRAN-491: Email Notifications for Customer Group Changes – HIGH priority, still in BACKLOG (Nour).\n- TRAN-1286: Security hotfix pending – recommend scheduling ASAP.\n- Site stability items still sitting in backlog: TRAN-641 (504 Gateway Timeouts), TRAN-1119 (New Relic response-time spikes), TRAN-1131 (UptimeRobot downtime review). Consider bundling into a performance/stability sprint.\n- Two unassigned tickets in backlog: TRAN-697 (Instant Purchase visibility), TRAN-674 (GA banner click tracking), TRAN-868 (AI Chatbot evaluation), TRAN-701 (Klaviyo event tracking) – need owners.\n\nITEMS NEEDING CUSTOMER INPUT/DECISIONS:\n- [Information Not Available] – no tickets are formally flagged as \'needs customer input\' in Jira. However, recommend raising with the client: (1) prioritisation of the large backlog, especially high-priority items TRAN-653 and TRAN-491; (2) approval/timing for the two Ready-for-Deployment items (TRAN-1275, TRAN-1283); (3) whether the Klaviyo campaign calendar (TRAN-1071) hold originates from their side.\n\nKEY TALKING POINTS & RECOMMENDATIONS:\n1. Lead with the AI Chatbot production launch (big win) and the follow-on optimization work (TRAN-1290).\n2. Confirm client sign-off/timing for the two deployment-ready features (shipping rules & rebuild kit purchase flow).\n3. Get a decision on backlog prioritisation, particularly the Highest/High priority items stuck in backlog.\n4. Internally: prioritise the SessionReaper security hotfix this week; chase Nexcess on TRAN-1027; clarify the Klaviyo calendar hold; assign owners to unassigned tickets.\n5. Do not mention internal eDesk account merge (TRAN-1292) or ticket IDs to the client.','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Transpart','<p>Hi Kelly,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Tuesday, July 21, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>The AI Chatbot has been deployed to your live site, and we\'ve begun the optimization phase.</li><li>Resolved the out-of-stock display issue so product availability now matches actual storefront behavior.</li><li>Fixed the issue where logging in as a customer on the live site redirected to the login page instead of the customer\'s session.</li><li>Completed a full round of code review, testing, and deployment.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Catalog update to implement bundle and configurable products.</li><li>Fixing the product kits import job that was failing near completion.</li><li>Applying a recommended security update to keep the platform protected.</li><li>Verifying the ShipStation and Klaviyo integrations are connected and working correctly.</li><li>Analyzing chatbot conversations to improve response quality following the launch.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>One staging environment item is currently pending a resolution from the hosting provider; we are following up with them directly.</li><li>The 6-month email campaign calendar is currently on hold — we\'d like to align with you on next steps during our call.</li><li>We\'d also like your input on prioritising several backlog items, including the order grid coloring for UPS shipping methods and email notifications for customer group changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>Estimated shipping rules and hold-status email notifications are ready for deployment — we\'d like to confirm timing with you.</li><li>The simplified purchase flow and display for Rebuild Kits / Packages is also ready for deployment, pending your go-ahead.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda</strong></p><ol><li>Review of completed work, including the AI Chatbot launch</li><li>Walkthrough and deployment approval for the two features ready to go live</li><li>Update on work in progress</li><li>Email campaign calendar — next steps</li><li>Backlog prioritisation and upcoming priorities</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>',NULL,NULL,'\"1. Wins & completed work review – AI Chatbot production launch, storefront fixes, and deployment round (15 min)\\n2. Deployment approvals – Estimated shipping rules & hold-status notifications; simplified Rebuild Kit purchase flow (20 min)\\n3. In-progress update – Bundle & configurable products, product kits import fix, security update, ShipStation/Klaviyo connection checks, chatbot optimization (20 min)\\n4. Klaviyo campaign calendar – reason for hold and plan to resume (15 min)\\n5. Backlog prioritisation – high-priority items (UPS order grid coloring, customer group email notifications) and site performance/stability items (20 min)\\n6. Open items, client questions, and next steps (15 min)\"','{\"other\": [{\"key\": \"TRAN-1275\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Configure Estimated Shipping Rules & Hold Status Email Notifications\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-21T16:32:52.211-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"TRAN-1283\", \"st