ess (Mostafa, HIGH), CMBR2-2170 Export active products de-de/it-it for bulk title update (Nour).\n- Ready For Dev (heavy load on Donia — 9 tickets assigned): CMBR2-2194 New Products flag / Welt Pixel Slider, CMBR2-2186 Color Filter improvements, CMBR2-2191 Mass Update Configurable Defaults (HIGH), CMBR2-2160 Best-sellers default sort, CMBR2-2189 Trusted Shops Trustbadge de-at/it-it, CMBR2-2185 Homepage CTA buttons IT/EN/DE (HIGH), CMBR2-2188 FAQ/Spec vertical layout (HIGH), CMBR2-2195 Magedelight FAQ save error (HIGH), CMBR2-2123 Mini-cart font rendering (Lowest). JP also has CMBR2-2196 PDP UX Improvements in Ready For Dev.\n\nREADY FOR REVIEW / QA (1):\n- CMBR2-2091: Adobe Commerce Security Patch APSB26-49 (HIGHEST, Nour) — currently QA on staging. This should be a top talking point; push for sign-off and production deployment window.\n\nREADY FOR DEPLOYMENT (7):\n- CMBR2-2174: B2B prices incorrectly showing VAT included (HIGHEST)\n- CMBR2-2187: Main image not updating on variant swatch selection (HIGHEST)\n- CMBR2-2173: PLP variant click not redirecting to PDP\n- CMBR2-2175: Automated weekly stock report to Benoit\n- CMBR2-2193: Accessory Upsell column in Firebear export\n- CMBR2-2179: \'Confezione\' button text truncation\n- CMBR2-1853: Multiple \'X\' characters in mobile menu\n\nBLOCKERS & RISKS:\n- No formally blocked tickets, but risks include: (1) deployment queue backlog with two Highest-priority customer-facing bugs awaiting release — agree on a deployment window with the client; (2) resource concentration risk: Donia carries 9+ Ready For Dev tickets including 4 High priority — consider load balancing; (3) security patch APSB26-49 still in staging QA — time-sensitive.\n\nITEMS NEEDING CUSTOMER INPUT: None formally flagged in Jira. However, recommend confirming: (a) approval/scheduling for the next production deployment covering the 7 ready items; (b) design confirmation for PDP UX improvements (CMBR2-2196) and FAQ vertical layout (CMBR2-2188) before dev starts; (c) confirmation that Benoit is the correct recipient for the weekly stock report (CMBR2-2175).\n\nKEY TALKING POINTS:\n1. Security patch APSB26-49 status and target production date.\n2. Batch deployment plan for the 7 ready items, especially the two Highest-priority PDP/B2B pricing bugs.\n3. Deployment process optimization (CMBR2-2169) — expected benefits and timeline.\n4. Prioritization of the large Ready For Dev backlog (which High items go first: CMBR2-2185, 2188, 2191, 2195).\n5. Cookie banner optimization progress and expected impact on analytics data quality (GA/Clarity).','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Cambro','<p>Hi Cambro team,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, August 5, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Fixed the corrupted product page header display on the English-Italian store.</li><li>Added the food safe icon to the selected products in bulk.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Optimizing the cookie banner to improve acceptance rates and analytics data quality.</li><li>Improving our deployment process to enable faster, more frequent releases.</li><li>Exporting active products for the German and Italian stores to prepare the bulk title update.</li><li>Queued for development: homepage \"New Products\" carousel button updates (IT, EN, DE), the new vertical FAQ/specification layout on product pages, product page UX improvements (accessories placement, sticky add-to-cart, and trust badges), Trusted Shops badge integration for the Austrian and Italian stores, color filter improvements, best-sellers sorting fix, and a fix for the FAQ management error in the admin.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>The latest Adobe Commerce security patch has been applied and is currently undergoing quality assurance on the staging environment. We\'d like to align on a production release window during our call.</li><li>Several completed fixes are ready for deployment, including the B2B pricing display fix (VAT), the product image update when selecting variant swatches, variant click-through to product pages, the automated weekly stock report, and a few smaller display fixes. We\'d like to confirm a deployment window with you.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>No blockers at this time. We would appreciate your confirmation on the upcoming deployment window and prioritization of the queued improvements.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda for Our Meeting</strong></p><ol><li>Review of completed work and items ready for deployment</li><li>Security patch status and production release scheduling</li><li>Prioritization of upcoming product page and homepage improvements</li><li>Open questions and next steps</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>','Status Update Before Our Meeting – Cambro','<p>Hi Cambro team,</p><p>Ahead of our meeting on Wednesday, August 5, 2026, here\'s a quick summary of where things stand:</p><p><strong>Completed Since Last Meeting</strong></p><ul><li>Fixed the corrupted product page header display on the English-Italian store.</li><li>Added the food safe icon to the selected products in bulk.</li></ul><p><strong>Currently In Progress</strong></p><ul><li>Optimizing the cookie banner to improve acceptance rates and analytics data quality.</li><li>Improving our deployment process to enable faster, more frequent releases.</li><li>Exporting active products for the German and Italian stores to prepare the bulk title update.</li><li>Queued for development: homepage \"New Products\" carousel button updates (IT, EN, DE), the new vertical FAQ/specification layout on product pages, product page UX improvements (accessories placement, sticky add-to-cart, and trust badges), Trusted Shops badge integration for the Austrian and Italian stores, color filter improvements, best-sellers sorting fix, and a fix for the FAQ management error in the admin.</li></ul><p><strong>Items Ready for Review</strong></p><ul><li>The latest Adobe Commerce security patch has been applied and is currently undergoing quality assurance on the staging environment. We\'d like to align on a production release window during our call.</li><li>Several completed fixes are ready for deployment, including the B2B pricing display fix (VAT), the product image update when selecting variant swatches, variant click-through to product pages, the automated weekly stock report, and a few smaller display fixes. We\'d like to confirm a deployment window with you.</li></ul><p><strong>Blockers / Items Needing Your Input</strong></p><ul><li>No blockers at this time. We would appreciate your confirmation on the upcoming deployment window and prioritization of the queued improvements.</li></ul><p><strong>Proposed Agenda for Our Meeting</strong></p><ol><li>Review of completed work and items ready for deployment</li><li>Security patch status and production release scheduling</li><li>Prioritization of upcoming product page and homepage improvements</li><li>Open questions and next steps</li></ol><p>Please let us know if you\'d like to add anything to the agenda. Looking forward to speaking with you.</p><p>Best,</p>','\"1. Welcome & review of completed items since last meeting (5 min)\\n2. Security patch APSB26-49 – QA status and production release scheduling (10 min)\\n3. Deployment plan for ready items, including the two highest-priority fixes (B2B VAT pricing display and product image/variant swatch bug) (15 min)\\n4. Prioritization of queued development work: homepage CTA updates, FAQ/specification vertical layout, PDP UX improvements, configurable defaults update, and FAQ module fix (15 min)\\n5. Progress updates: cookie banner optimization, deployment process improvements, and bulk product title export for de-de/it-it (10 min)\\n6. Open items, customer questions, and next steps (5-10 min)\"','{\"other\": [{\"key\": \"CMBR2-1853\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Multiple “X” characters displayed at top of mobile menu (hamburger drawer)\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-05T05:39:21.779-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Low\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2175\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Create an automated weekly stock report and configure it to be sent to Benoit\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-04T17:28:41.109-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2193\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Add Accessory Upsell Column to Firebear Product Export\", \"updated\": \"2026-08-04T15:44:54.892-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2174\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"B2B Customer: Product prices incorrectly display with VAT included\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T18:22:32.212-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Highest\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2173\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Clicking product variants on PLP does not redirect to PDP\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T18:12:25.096-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Medium\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2179\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Text truncated on the \\\"Confezione\\\" button under order quantity filter.\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T18:07:19.470-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Low\"}, {\"key\": \"CMBR2-2187\", \"status\": \"Ready for Deployment\", \"summary\": \"Main product image does not update when selecting different variant swatches on PDP\", \"updated\": \"2026-07-31T10:50:29.477-0400\", \"assignee\": \"Mostafa Naguib\", \"priority\": \"Highest\"}], \"in_progress\": [{\"key\": \"CMBR2-2194\", \"status\": \"Ready For Dev\", \"summary\": \"New Products flag not reflecting on homepage 