ues, specifically increased script errors and server slowdown, are the primary cause contributing to Checkout → Purchase abandonment spike observed. This issue caused disconnects between user activity and transactions, reflected by compressed conversion rates and cluttered user paths identified by numerous friction indicators.\n\nThe impact is significant, evident by its magnitude (**15.1%** increase month-over-month) contributing to substantial potential revenue losses on high traffic days. These friction-generated aberrations restricted transactional flow despite maintained session activity.\n\nImmediate action should involve enhancing backend server efficiency and stabilizing frontend interactions to minimize script errors and reduce friction scores. Addressing these vulnerabilities will be critical to regaining purchase confidence and capitalizing on session retention and conversion aspirations.','openai/gpt-4o','2026-07-22 02:00:39','2026-07-22 02:00:39','internal',0),(9,22,'1. **Adobe Commerce AOV**: Increased to $359.72 on July 9 from $287.74 on July 8, indicating purchase pattern change\n2. **GA4 vs Adobe Commerce**: On July 11, GA4 shows 2909 sessions while Adobe Commerce notes only 21 orders, demonstrating misalignment\n3. **Clarity Correlation**: Dead clicks peaked at 168 on July 12, correlating with a spike in script errors of 5024\n4. **Klaviyo Campaigns**: While primary revenues are attributed to other channels, email flows like \'Email sign up\' produced meaningful revenue shifts e.g., $1085.19 on July 18\n5. **Traffic Source Shift**: Organic search yielded notable revenue on July 17, with $1376.51 via Adobe Commerce.','**What Happened**\nAverage order value (AOV) increased by **10.4%**, rising from **$267.09** to **$294.75** over the past 30 days, identified on **July 22**.\n\n| Metric | Prior Period | Anomaly Period | Change |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Average Order Value (AOV) | $267.09 | $294.75 | +10.4% |\n| Revenue** | Sum | Calculation | In